      <h1 id="stage-24-drafts-and-localization" class="group scroll-mt-20">Stage 24: Drafts and localization<a href="#stage-24-drafts-and-localization" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h1>
      <p>Prepare the guide for review and translation. Declare the language of each topic and map, identify text that stays untranslated, set the direction of a Hebrew phrase, and supply a glossary sort key.</p>
      <p>Add review comments, content that requires cleanup, revision metadata, and a change history. The gate reports the review markup as warnings. Stage 25 adds rules that require you to resolve it before release.</p>
      <p><strong>Optional module.</strong> See <a href="/dogsbay-xml-dita-tutorial-docs/start-here/learning-path">Choose a learning path</a> for the starting checkpoint and the next core lesson.</p>
      <p><strong>Time:</strong> about 30 minutes. <strong>You need:</strong> stage 23 complete.</p>
      <p>Recorded diagnostic examples below come from earlier runs. File counts, paths, and stage numbers can differ. Run the gate for your current checkout.</p>
      <h2 id="step-1-language-and-translation" class="group scroll-mt-20">Step 1: Language and translation<a href="#step-1-language-and-translation" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <Steps>
      <Step>
      <strong>Add </strong><strong><code>xml:lang="en-GB"</code></strong><strong> to every root element</strong>
      <CodeBlock code={"--- a/topics/what-is-audacity.dita\n+++ b/topics/what-is-audacity.dita\n@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@\n \u003c?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n \u003c!DOCTYPE concept PUBLIC \"-//OASIS//DTD DITA Concept//EN\" \"concept.dtd\">\n \n-\u003cconcept id=\"what-is-audacity\">\n+\u003cconcept id=\"what-is-audacity\" xml:lang=\"en-GB\">\n   \u003ctitle>What is \u003ckeyword keyref=\"product-name\"/>?\u003c/title>\n   \u003cshortdesc>\u003ckeyword keyref=\"product-name\"/> is a free, open-source audio editor and recorder for Windows, macOS and Linux.\u003c/shortdesc>\n   \u003cprolog>"} lang="diff" title="topics/what-is-audacity.dita" />
      <p>The same one-line change goes on the root element of all 35 <code>.dita</code> and <code>.ditamap</code> files on the branch: every topic, every glossary entry, the shared topics in <code>shared/</code>, the assessment in <code>learning/</code>, and all nine maps. The <code>compare</code> link at the end shows them all.</p>
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Read it</strong>
      <ul>
      <li><code>xml:lang</code> is XML's own language attribute, in the <code>xml</code> namespace, so it needs no declaration. Its value is a BCP 47 language tag: <code>en-GB</code> for British English, <code>de</code> for German, <code>pt-BR</code> for Brazilian Portuguese. An element without one inherits its parent's, so one attribute on the root covers the file.</li>
      <li>DITA-OT reads it. The map's language chooses the generated text in the output, the <em>CAUTION</em> of a hazard statement, the <em>Table 1</em> of a table title, the headings of the index, and the sort order of the index and glossary in the PDF. Each HTML5 page carries the topic's language as <code>&lt;html lang="en-gb"&gt;</code>, which is what a screen reader uses to choose a voice.</li>
      <li>A translation tool reads it too: the source language of every file it is given, and the target language once it writes the translated copy.</li>
      </ul>
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Mark what must not be translated</strong>
      <CodeBlock code={"--- a/keydefs-product.ditamap\n+++ b/keydefs-product.ditamap\n@@ -1,13 +1,13 @@\n \u003c?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n \u003c!DOCTYPE map PUBLIC \"-//OASIS//DTD DITA Map//EN\" \"map.dtd\">\n \n-\u003cmap>\n+\u003cmap xml:lang=\"en-GB\">\n   \u003ctitle>Product key definitions\u003c/title>\n \n   \u003ckeydef keys=\"product-name\">\n     \u003ctopicmeta>\n       \u003ckeywords>\n-        \u003ckeyword>Audacity\u003c/keyword>\n+        \u003ckeyword translate=\"no\">Audacity\u003c/keyword>\n       \u003c/keywords>\n     \u003c/topicmeta>\n   \u003c/keydef>\n@@ -26,7 +26,7 @@\n   \u003ckeydef keys=\"project-extension\">\n     \u003ctopicmeta>\n       \u003ckeywords>\n-        \u003ckeyword>.aup3\u003c/keyword>\n+        \u003ckeyword translate=\"no\">.aup3\u003c/keyword>\n       \u003c/keywords>\n     \u003c/topicmeta>\n   \u003c/keydef>"} lang="diff" title="keydefs-product.ditamap" />
      <p><code>translate="no"</code> on a <code>&lt;keyword&gt;</code> says its text is not to be translated. The product name and the project extension are marked once, where their values live; every <code>&lt;keyword keyref="product-name"/&gt;</code> in the topics pulls the marked text in. <code>translate</code> takes <code>yes</code> or <code>no</code> and inherits, so it can go on a block to cover everything inside.</p>
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Mark the code and the commands</strong>
      <CodeBlock code={"--- a/topics/scripting-reference.dita\n+++ b/topics/scripting-reference.dita\n@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@\n \u003c?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n \u003c!DOCTYPE reference PUBLIC \"-//OASIS//DTD DITA Reference//EN\" \"reference.dtd\">\n \n-\u003creference id=\"scripting-reference\">\n+\u003creference id=\"scripting-reference\" xml:lang=\"en-GB\">\n   \u003ctitle>Scripting commands\u003c/title>\n   \u003cshortdesc>The scripting commands most useful for batch work, their parameters and the responses they return.\u003c/shortdesc>\n   \u003cprolog>\n@@ -42,7 +42,7 @@\n     \u003c/section>\n     \u003crefsyn>\n       \u003ctitle>Commands\u003c/title>\n-      \u003cparml>\n+      \u003cparml translate=\"no\">\n         \u003cplentry>\n           \u003cpt>\n             \u003ccmdname>SelectAll:\u003c/cmdname>\n@@ -68,7 +68,7 @@\n       \u003ctitle>Responses\u003c/title>\n       \u003cp>Every reply ends with a status line.\n       Success looks like \u003cmsgph>BatchCommand finished: OK\u003c/msgph>; a failure names the command:\u003c/p>\n-      \u003cmsgblock>Export2: Filename=episode.mp3 NumChannels=1\n+      \u003cmsgblock translate=\"no\">Export2: Filename=episode.mp3 NumChannels=1\n BatchCommand finished: Failed!\u003c/msgblock>\n       \u003cp>The \u003capiname>send\u003c/apiname> function in the sample script (\u003cxref href=\"../samples/export-mp3.py\" scope=\"external\" format=\"py\">export-mp3.py\u003c/xref>) returns the whole reply; check it for \u003cmsgnum>Failed!\u003c/msgnum> before sending the next command.\u003c/p>\n     \u003c/section>"} lang="diff" title="topics/scripting-reference.dita" />
      <CodeBlock code={"--- a/topics/exporting-from-a-script.dita\n+++ b/topics/exporting-from-a-script.dita\n@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@\n \u003c?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n \u003c!DOCTYPE task PUBLIC \"-//OASIS//DTD DITA Task//EN\" \"task.dtd\">\n \n-\u003ctask id=\"exporting-from-a-script\">\n+\u003ctask id=\"exporting-from-a-script\" xml:lang=\"en-GB\">\n   \u003ctitle>Exporting from a script\u003c/title>\n   \u003cshortdesc>Enable mod-script-pipe, then normalize and export the open project from a Python script.\u003c/shortdesc>\n   \u003cprolog>\n@@ -31,13 +31,13 @@\n       \u003cstep>\n         \u003ccmd>Save the sample script as \u003cfilepath>export-mp3.py\u003c/filepath>.\u003c/cmd>\n         \u003cinfo>\n-          \u003ccodeblock outputclass=\"language-python\">\u003ccoderef href=\"../samples/export-mp3.py\"/>\u003c/codeblock>\n+          \u003ccodeblock outputclass=\"language-python\" translate=\"no\">\u003ccoderef href=\"../samples/export-mp3.py\"/>\u003c/codeblock>\n         \u003c/info>\n       \u003c/step>\n       \u003cstep>\n         \u003ccmd>Run it, naming the output file.\u003c/cmd>\n         \u003cinfo>\n-          \u003cscreen>\u003cuserinput>python3 export-mp3.py episode.mp3\u003c/userinput>\n+          \u003cscreen translate=\"no\">\u003cuserinput>python3 export-mp3.py episode.mp3\u003c/userinput>\n \u003csystemoutput>BatchCommand finished: OK\n BatchCommand finished: OK\n BatchCommand finished: OK\u003c/systemoutput>\u003c/screen>"} lang="diff" title="topics/exporting-from-a-script.dita" />
      <p>The parameter list, the message block, the code block and the screen from stage 22 are all things a translator must leave alone. The DITA specification says that many of the code elements, <code>&lt;codeblock&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;screen&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;cmdname&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;parmname&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;varname&gt;</code> among them, are <code>translate="no"</code> by default, but explicit attributes also record the intent for tools that do not apply the DITA translation defaults. Marking the whole <code>&lt;parml&gt;</code> keeps the <code>&lt;pd&gt;</code> descriptions in English as well as the <code>&lt;pt&gt;</code> terms; mark each <code>&lt;pt&gt;</code> instead if the descriptions are to be translated.</p>
      </Step>
      </Steps>
      <h2 id="step-2-direction-and-sort-order" class="group scroll-mt-20">Step 2: Direction and sort order<a href="#step-2-direction-and-sort-order" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <Steps>
      <Step>
      <strong>Edit </strong><strong><code>topics/what-is-digital-audio.dita</code></strong>
      <CodeBlock code={"--- a/topics/what-is-digital-audio.dita\n+++ b/topics/what-is-digital-audio.dita\n@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@\n \u003c?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n \u003c!DOCTYPE concept PUBLIC \"-//OASIS//DTD DITA Concept//EN\" \"concept.dtd\">\n \n-\u003cconcept id=\"what-is-digital-audio\">\n+\u003cconcept id=\"what-is-digital-audio\" xml:lang=\"en-GB\">\n   \u003ctitle>What is digital audio?\u003c/title>\n   \u003cshortdesc>Digital audio is sound stored as numbers: samples taken thousands of times a second at a chosen precision.\u003c/shortdesc>\n   \u003cprolog>\n@@ -26,6 +26,7 @@\n         \u003cindexterm>decibel\u003cindex-see-also>amplitude\u003c/index-see-also>\u003c/indexterm>\n         \u003cindexterm>amplitude\u003c/indexterm>\n         \u003cindexterm>\u003cindex-sort-as>clipping\u003c/index-sort-as>Clipping (distortion)\u003c/indexterm>\n+        \u003cindexterm>dB\u003cindex-see>decibel\u003c/index-see>\u003c/indexterm>\n       \u003c/keywords>\n     \u003c/metadata>\n   \u003c/prolog>\n@@ -133,6 +134,7 @@\n         \u003c/dlentry>\n       \u003c/dl>\n       \u003clq reftitle=\"The Audacity Manual\">Audio is measured in decibels because the ear hears ratios, not differences.\u003c/lq>\n+      \u003cp>The same idea in Hebrew, for a right-to-left example: \u003cph xml:lang=\"he\" dir=\"rtl\">האוזן שומעת יחסים\u003c/ph> (the ear hears ratios).\u003c/p>\n     \u003c/section>\n   \u003c/conbody>\n   \u003crelated-links>"} lang="diff" title="topics/what-is-digital-audio.dita" />
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Read it</strong>
      <ul>
      <li><code>xml:lang="he"</code> on a <code>&lt;ph&gt;</code> overrides the root's <code>en-GB</code> for that phrase alone. <code>dir="rtl"</code> says the phrase runs right to left; the values are <code>ltr</code>, <code>rtl</code>, <code>lro</code> and <code>rlo</code>, the last two overriding the characters' own direction. Hebrew and Arabic letters carry their direction, so the attribute matters most where a phrase mixes them with digits and punctuation, and it is what a stylesheet keys on.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;index-see&gt;</code>, from stage 13, adds an index entry that redirects: <em>dB, see decibel</em>. The abbreviation gets its own line in the index and the reader is sent to the entry that has the page numbers.</li>
      </ul>
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Edit </strong><strong><code>topics/glossary/audio-units.dita</code></strong>
      <CodeBlock code={"--- a/topics/glossary/audio-units.dita\n+++ b/topics/glossary/audio-units.dita\n@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@\n \u003c?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n \u003c!DOCTYPE glossgroup PUBLIC \"-//OASIS//DTD DITA Glossary Group//EN\" \"glossgroup.dtd\">\n \n-\u003cglossgroup id=\"audio-units\">\n+\u003cglossgroup id=\"audio-units\" xml:lang=\"en-GB\">\n   \u003ctitle>Units\u003c/title>\n   \u003cprolog>\n     \u003cauthor type=\"creator\">The Audacity tutorial team\u003c/author>\n@@ -13,7 +13,7 @@\n     \u003c/metadata>\n   \u003c/prolog>\n   \u003cglossentry id=\"gl-decibel\">\n-    \u003cglossterm>decibel\u003c/glossterm>\n+    \u003cglossterm>\u003csort-as value=\"decibel\"/>dB (decibel)\u003c/glossterm>\n     \u003cglossdef>A logarithmic unit for the ratio between two levels. In audio editing, 0 dB is the loudest level a file can hold, and quieter sounds are negative.\u003c/glossdef>\n     \u003cprolog>\n       \u003cauthor type=\"creator\">The Audacity tutorial team\u003c/author>"} lang="diff" title="topics/glossary/audio-units.dita" />
      <p>The displayed term is now <em>dB (decibel)</em>, and <code>&lt;sort-as value="decibel"/&gt;</code> tells a sorted glossary to place it as if it read <em>decibel</em>. <code>&lt;sort-as&gt;</code> is a DITA 1.3 element allowed in titles and glossary terms. It is for the cases a plain sort gets wrong: a term that starts with a symbol, a digit or an abbreviation, or a language where the sort key is not the displayed characters, as with Japanese kanji sorted by their reading. <code>&lt;index-sort-as&gt;</code> on the <em>Clipping (distortion)</em> entry, three lines up in the same prolog, is the index term's equivalent.</p>
      </Step>
      </Steps>
      <h2 id="step-3-review-markup-and-a-change-history" class="group scroll-mt-20">Step 3: Review markup and a change history<a href="#step-3-review-markup-and-a-change-history" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <Steps>
      <Step>
      <strong>Edit </strong><strong><code>topics/exporting-audio.dita</code></strong>
      <CodeBlock code={"--- a/topics/exporting-audio.dita\n+++ b/topics/exporting-audio.dita\n@@ -1,13 +1,14 @@\n \u003c?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n \u003c!DOCTYPE task PUBLIC \"-//OASIS//DTD DITA Task//EN\" \"task.dtd\">\n \n-\u003ctask id=\"exporting-audio\">\n+\u003ctask id=\"exporting-audio\" xml:lang=\"en-GB\" status=\"changed\">\n   \u003ctitle>Exporting audio\u003c/title>\n   \u003cshortdesc>Export a finished project as a WAV, MP3, OGG or FLAC file that other programs and devices can play.\u003c/shortdesc>\n   \u003cprolog>\n     \u003cauthor type=\"creator\">The Audacity tutorial team\u003c/author>\n     \u003ccritdates>\n       \u003ccreated date=\"2026-01-22\"/>\n+      \u003crevised modified=\"2026-03-05\"/>\n     \u003c/critdates>\n     \u003cmetadata>\n       \u003caudience type=\"user\" experiencelevel=\"novice\"/>\n@@ -22,6 +23,13 @@\n         \u003cindexterm>audio formats\u003cindexterm>MP3\u003c/indexterm>\u003cindexterm>WAV\u003c/indexterm>\u003c/indexterm>\n       \u003c/keywords>\n     \u003c/metadata>\n+    \u003cchange-historylist>\n+      \u003cchange-item>\n+        \u003cchange-person>The Audacity tutorial team\u003c/change-person>\n+        \u003cchange-completed>2026-03-05\u003c/change-completed>\n+        \u003cchange-summary>Marked the metadata-tags step as new in 3.4.\u003c/change-summary>\n+      \u003c/change-item>\n+    \u003c/change-historylist>\n   \u003c/prolog>\n   \u003ctaskbody>\n     \u003cprereq>\n@@ -67,6 +75,7 @@\n       \u003c/step>\n     \u003c/steps>\n     \u003cresult>\n+      \u003cdraft-comment author=\"reviewer\" time=\"2026-03-05\" disposition=\"open\">Check the 3.4 export dialog: is the metadata tags step still a separate dialog?\u003c/draft-comment>\n       \u003cp>The exported file is in the folder you chose.\n       The project itself is unchanged.\u003c/p>\n     \u003c/result>"} lang="diff" title="topics/exporting-audio.dita" />
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Read it</strong>
      <ul>
      <li><code>status="changed"</code> on the root says the topic changed since the last release. The values are <code>new</code>, <code>changed</code>, <code>deleted</code> and <code>unchanged</code>, and the attribute is allowed on most elements, so a single row or paragraph can carry it. Nothing renders it by default; a DITAVAL or a report can select on it.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;revised modified="2026-03-05"/&gt;</code> joins the <code>&lt;created&gt;</code> from stage 12 in <code>&lt;critdates&gt;</code>. The content model is <code>created?</code> then <code>revised*</code>, in that order, one <code>&lt;revised&gt;</code> per revision.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;change-historylist&gt;</code> is DITA 1.3's structured change log, in the <code>&lt;prolog&gt;</code> after <code>&lt;metadata&gt;</code>. Each <code>&lt;change-item&gt;</code> holds who, <code>&lt;change-person&gt;</code>, when, <code>&lt;change-completed&gt;</code>, and what, <code>&lt;change-summary&gt;</code>. The other children are <code>&lt;change-organization&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;change-revisionid&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;change-request-reference&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;change-started&gt;</code>.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;draft-comment&gt;</code> is a note to the reviewer, in the flow where it applies. <code>author</code> and <code>time</code> say who and when; <code>disposition</code> tracks it, <code>open</code>, <code>accepted</code>, <code>rejected</code>, <code>deferred</code>, <code>duplicate</code>, <code>reopened</code>, <code>unassigned</code> or <code>completed</code>. DITA-OT drops draft comments from the output unless you ask for them, which step 4 shows.</li>
      </ul>
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Edit </strong><strong><code>topics/podcast-production-workflow.dita</code></strong>
      <CodeBlock code={"--- a/topics/podcast-production-workflow.dita\n+++ b/topics/podcast-production-workflow.dita\n@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@\n \u003c?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n \u003c!DOCTYPE concept PUBLIC \"-//OASIS//DTD DITA Concept//EN\" \"concept.dtd\">\n \n-\u003cconcept id=\"podcast-production-workflow\">\n+\u003cconcept id=\"podcast-production-workflow\" xml:lang=\"en-GB\">\n   \u003ctitle>Podcast production workflow\u003c/title>\n   \u003cshortdesc>A typical order of work for a spoken-word podcast: prepare, record, clean up, level and export.\u003c/shortdesc>\n   \u003cprolog>\n@@ -51,6 +51,7 @@\n         \u003cli>\u003cb>\u003cterm keyref=\"gl-compression\">Compression\u003c/term>\u003c/b>: even out volume differences (threshold -18 dB, ratio 3:1).\u003c/li>\n         \u003cli>\u003cb>Export\u003c/b>: MP3 at 128 kbps mono for distribution, by hand or from a script (\u003cxref keyref=\"scripting\"/>).\u003c/li>\n       \u003c/ol>\n+      \u003crequired-cleanup remap=\"table\">Target loudness per platform: Spotify -14 LUFS, Apple -16 LUFS, YouTube -14 LUFS. Turn into a table once the list is confirmed.\u003c/required-cleanup>\n     \u003c/section>\n     \u003csection audience=\"beginner\">\n       \u003ctitle>Getting started with podcasting\u003c/title>"} lang="diff" title="topics/podcast-production-workflow.dita" />
      <p><code>&lt;required-cleanup&gt;</code> marks content that is not in its final form. It is allowed almost anywhere and holds almost anything, which is the point: it is where content goes that does not yet fit the grammar of its place. <code>remap="table"</code> records what it should become. Like a draft comment, it is dropped from the output by default.</p>
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Edit </strong><strong><code>topics/effects-reference.dita</code></strong>
      <CodeBlock code={"--- a/topics/effects-reference.dita\n+++ b/topics/effects-reference.dita\n@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@\n \u003c?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n \u003c!DOCTYPE reference PUBLIC \"-//OASIS//DTD DITA Reference//EN\" \"reference.dtd\">\n \n-\u003creference id=\"effects-reference\">\n+\u003creference id=\"effects-reference\" xml:lang=\"en-GB\">\n   \u003ctitle>Effects reference\u003c/title>\n   \u003cshortdesc>The built-in effects, what each one does, and the parameters that matter.\u003c/shortdesc>\n   \u003cprolog>\n@@ -17,6 +17,7 @@\n         \u003ckeyword>Amplify\u003c/keyword>\n         \u003ckeyword>Compressor\u003c/keyword>\n         \u003ckeyword>Normalize\u003c/keyword>\n+        \u003ckeyword>Loudness Normalization\u003c/keyword>\n         \u003cindexterm>effects\u003cindexterm>reference\u003c/indexterm>\u003c/indexterm>\n       \u003c/keywords>\n     \u003c/metadata>\n@@ -68,6 +69,11 @@\n             \u003centry>Sets the peak amplitude to a target level and optionally removes DC offset.\u003c/entry>\n             \u003centry>Peak amplitude (dB), typically -1.0; \u003cuicontrol>Remove DC offset\u003c/uicontrol>.\u003c/entry>\n           \u003c/row>\n+          \u003crow rev=\"3.4\" status=\"new\">\n+            \u003centry>Loudness Normalization\u003c/entry>\n+            \u003centry>Sets the perceived loudness of the selection to a target, for podcast platforms that specify one.\u003c/entry>\n+            \u003centry>Target (LUFS), typically -16 for podcasts; \u003cuicontrol>Normalize\u003c/uicontrol> to perceived loudness or RMS.\u003c/entry>\n+          \u003c/row>\n           \u003crow>\n             \u003centry>Fade In, Fade Out\u003c/entry>\n             \u003centry>Ramps the volume of the selection up from silence, or down to it.\u003c/entry>"} lang="diff" title="topics/effects-reference.dita" />
      <p>A new effect for the next release, as a table row. <code>rev="3.4"</code> is the revision mark from stage 14, which <code>filters/review.ditaval</code> flags; <code>status="new"</code> says the same thing to a tool that reads status rather than revisions. The new effect's name also joins the <code>&lt;keywords&gt;</code> in the prolog, which the metadata policy from stage 13 asks for.</p>
      </Step>
      </Steps>
      <h2 id="step-4-readme-and-the-gate" class="group scroll-mt-20">Step 4: README and the gate<a href="#step-4-readme-and-the-gate" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <Steps>
      <Step>
      <strong>Change the "You are on" line</strong>
      <CodeBlock code={"--- a/README.md\n+++ b/README.md\n@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@\n \n Build a guide through 27 stages. Maps begin at stage 02; HTML publication begins at stage 03.\n \n-You are on stage 23: learning.\n+You are on stage 24: drafts and localization.\n \n ## Stages\n "} lang="diff" title="README.md" />
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Format and check</strong>
      <CodeBlock code={"dogsbay-xml format -i topics/*.dita topics/glossary/*.dita shared/*.dita *.ditamap\nscripts/check-stage.sh"} lang="bash" />
      <CodeBlock code={"== validate-project  /home/you/audacity-guide ==\n/home/you/audacity-guide/learning/check-your-understanding.dita:\n  -1:-1  error: Validation failed: /home/you/audacity-guide/learning/learningAssessment.dtd (No such file or directory)\n42 file(s): 41 valid, 1 invalid.\n\n== validate learning/ against the DITA-OT catalog ==\nVALID\n\n== project-health  /home/you/audacity-guide ==\nRoot map: audacity-guide.ditamap (project config); house rules: none (none configured)\nAuthoring leftovers (2; warnings):\n  /home/you/audacity-guide/topics/exporting-audio.dita:78  draft-comment: Check the 3.4 export dialog: is the metadata tags step still a separate dialog?\n  /home/you/audacity-guide/topics/podcast-production-workflow.dita:54  required-cleanup: Target loudness per platform: Spotify -14 LUFS, Apple -16 LUFS, YouTube -14 LUFS. Turn into a table…\nProject is healthy: valid, no broken references, keys, orphans, or broken element ids.\n\n== validate-conditions  /home/you/audacity-guide  (scheme: subject-scheme.ditamap) ==\n42 file(s): 42 pass, 0 with violations.\n\n== build  project.json -> /tmp/check-stage-\u003cpid> ==\nall deliverables built\n\nSTAGE OK"} lang="plaintext" />
      <p><code>project-health</code> now has something to say. <em>Authoring leftovers</em> is its name for review markup, and it counts the draft comment and the required cleanup, two, with the file and line of each. They are warnings: the project is still healthy, the gate still prints <code>STAGE OK</code>, and the markup goes into the repository as the record of what is unfinished. Stage 25 adds a house rule that makes the same two findings failures, so that they cannot reach a release.</p>
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Read the review build</strong> Run <code>dita --project=project.json</code> to create the following paths under your project directory, or use <code>out/</code> under the gate's build directory.
      <p>The <code>review</code> deliverable from stage 14 flags revision <code>3.4</code>, so in <code>out/review/topics/effects-reference.html</code> the new row carries the flag's color:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"\u003ctr style=\"color:#b00020;\" class=\"row\">\n\u003ctd class=\"entry\" headers=\"effects-reference__entry__1\">Loudness Normalization\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd class=\"entry\" headers=\"effects-reference__entry__2\">Sets the perceived loudness of the selection to a target, for podcast platforms that specify one.\u003c/td>\n\u003ctd class=\"entry\" headers=\"effects-reference__entry__3\">Target (LUFS), typically -16 for podcasts; \u003cspan class=\"ph uicontrol\">Normalize\u003c/span> to perceived loudness or RMS.\u003c/td>\n\u003c/tr>"} lang="plaintext" />
      <p>The <code>[new in 3.4]</code> start-flag text is not on the row: DITA-OT puts flag text only where text can go, and a table row has no place for it outside its cells. On the step that stage 14 marked, in <code>out/review/topics/exporting-audio.html</code>, both the color and the text appear:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"\u003cspan style=\"color:#b00020;\" class=\"ph cmd\">[new in 3.4]Fill in the \u003cspan class=\"keyword wintitle\">Edit Metadata Tags\u003c/span> dialog and click \u003cspan class=\"ph uicontrol\">OK\u003c/span>.\u003c/span>"} lang="plaintext" />
      <p>The draft comment is in neither build, nor is the required cleanup: DITA-OT drops <code>&lt;draft-comment&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;required-cleanup&gt;</code> unless the build asks for them with <code>args.draft=yes</code>. A search for the comment's text across every HTML5 deliverable the gate built, <code>grep -rl 'metadata tags step' /tmp/check-stage-&lt;pid&gt;</code>, prints nothing. To see them, build the review map once with the parameter:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"dita -i audacity-guide.ditamap -f html5 --filter=filters/review.ditaval -o /tmp/review-draft --args.draft=yes"} lang="bash" />
      <CodeBlock code={"\u003cdiv class=\"draft-comment\" style=\"background-color: #99FF99; border: 1pt black solid;\">\u003cstrong>Draft comment: \u003c/strong>reviewer open 2026-03-05\u003cbr>Check the 3.4 export dialog: is the metadata tags step still a separate dialog?\u003c/div>\n\u003cdiv class=\"required-cleanup\" style=\"background-color: #FFFF99; color:#CC3333; border: 1pt black solid;\">\u003cstrong>Required cleanup: \u003c/strong>[table] Target loudness per platform: Spotify -14 LUFS, Apple -16 LUFS, YouTube -14 LUFS. Turn into a table once the list is confirmed.\u003c/div>"} lang="plaintext" />
      <p>The comment and the cleanup are rendered in place, boxed and colored, with the author, disposition and date. Use <code>args.draft=yes</code> to include this markup during review. Resolve it before release.</p>
      </Step>
      </Steps>
      <p>Test an invalid value. Change the new row in <code>topics/effects-reference.dita</code> to <code>status="draft"</code>, a value that reads well and does not exist, and run the gate with <code>SKIP_BUILD=1</code>:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"== validate-project  /home/you/audacity-guide ==\n/home/you/audacity-guide/learning/check-your-understanding.dita:\n  -1:-1  error: Validation failed: /home/you/audacity-guide/learning/learningAssessment.dtd (No such file or directory)\n/home/you/audacity-guide/topics/effects-reference.dita:\n  74:41  error: Attribute \"status\" with value \"draft\" must have a value from the list \"changed deleted new unchanged -dita-use-conref-target \".\n42 file(s): 40 valid, 2 invalid.\nFAIL: validation errors"} lang="plaintext" />
      <p><code>status</code> is an enumerated attribute in the DTD, unlike <code>rev</code>, which takes any string. The four values, plus <code>-dita-use-conref-target</code>, which every enumerated attribute accepts for conref, are the whole vocabulary; a workflow state such as <em>draft</em> or <em>in review</em> belongs in a <code>&lt;draft-comment disposition&gt;</code> or in <code>&lt;change-historylist&gt;</code>, not in <code>status</code>.</p>
      <p>The formatter used for the recorded examples escaped ampersands repeatedly, changing <code>&amp;amp;</code> to <code>&amp;amp;amp;</code> on a subsequent pass. Check the diff after formatting with your installed version. Preserve valid XML escaping when an ampersand is required; use <em>and</em> where it expresses the intended wording.</p>
      <p>After each error exercise, undo the deliberate change and rerun the gate. Confirm that it prints <code>STAGE OK</code> before continuing.</p>
      <h2 id="what-you-learned" class="group scroll-mt-20">What you learned<a href="#what-you-learned" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <ul>
      <li><code>xml:lang</code> on every root; <code>translate="no"</code> on the product keys and the code; <code>xml:lang</code> and <code>dir="rtl"</code> on a phrase.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;sort-as&gt;</code> in a glossary term, <code>&lt;index-see&gt;</code> for an abbreviation.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;draft-comment author time disposition&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;required-cleanup remap&gt;</code>: review markup that DITA-OT drops unless <code>args.draft=yes</code>.</li>
      <li><code>status</code> on a topic or a row, <code>&lt;revised&gt;</code> beside <code>&lt;created&gt;</code>, and <code>&lt;change-historylist&gt;</code> with <code>&lt;change-item&gt;</code>.</li>
      <li><code>project-health</code> reports review markup as <em>Authoring leftovers</em>, warnings until a house rule says otherwise.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2 id="next-lesson" class="group scroll-mt-20">Next lesson<a href="#next-lesson" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <p>Continue with <a href="/dogsbay-xml-dita-tutorial-docs/part-5-governance/stage-25-house-rules">Stage 25: house rules</a>.</p>
